    intro="PRINCE2 vs Agile is less a contest than a comparison of two different jobs: PRINCE2 is a method for governing a project (who decides, when and within what limits), while Agile is a way of delivering the work in short, feedback-driven cycles. Many organisations that use PRINCE2 also run Agile teams, and PRINCE2 Agile is the official guidance for combining them. This guide compares the two side by side, maps roles and documents across, and shows step by step how to run Agile delivery inside PRINCE2 governance, with an illustrative worked example.",
