    faq=[
        ("Is PRINCE2 agile or waterfall?", "Neither by definition. PRINCE2 is a governance method whose stages are decision points for the board, not technical phases. It is often paired with sequential delivery, but the work inside each stage can be delivered in sprints."),
        ("Can PRINCE2 and Scrum be used together?", "Yes. PRINCE2 provides the governance layer (business case, project board, stages and tolerances) and the Scrum Team delivers inside it, with work packages expressed as sprint or release goals."),
        ("What is PRINCE2 Agile?", "Official guidance from PeopleCert on running Agile delivery within PRINCE2 governance. It was first published in 2015, and a new version aligned with PRINCE2 7 was released in 2025. It covers frameworks such as Scrum and Kanban and how to tailor PRINCE2's principles, practices and processes for Agile work."),
        ("What does fix and flex mean in PRINCE2 Agile?", "It means fixing time and cost and letting scope and some quality criteria flex within agreed tolerances. Benefits and risk can be fixed or flexed depending on the project. In practice, Must-have scope is protected and lower-priority features are deferred if time runs short."),
        ("Does PRINCE2 have a Scrum Master or Product Owner?", "Not as named roles. In PRINCE2 Agile, the Product Owner usually works for or alongside the senior user, and the Scrum Master supports a team that delivers work packages under the team manager role."),
        ("Who owns PRINCE2?", "PRINCE2 originated with the UK government and is now owned by PeopleCert, which acquired AXELOS in 2021. PeopleCert also owns PRINCE2 Agile and runs the certification exams. The current edition of the core method is PRINCE2 7, published in 2023."),
        ("How does management by exception work in an Agile project?", "The board sets tolerances for time, cost, scope and other targets, and the team works freely within them. The project manager forecasts against those tolerances each sprint, usually from velocity and the remaining Must-have backlog, and escalates only when a tolerance is forecast to be exceeded."),
        ("Is PRINCE2 still relevant?", "Yes, particularly in the UK, Europe, Australia and the public sector. PeopleCert updated the core method in 2023 and PRINCE2 Agile in 2025."),
        ("Which is better for my career, PRINCE2 or an Agile certification?", "It depends on your market. PRINCE2 is widely requested for project manager roles in the UK, Europe and the public sector; Scrum and other Agile certifications are common in product and technology roles. Many project managers hold one of each."),
        ("Do I need PRINCE2 before taking PRINCE2 Agile?", "Not necessarily for the Foundation level, but prerequisites can differ by level and version and PeopleCert sets them. Check PeopleCert's current requirements before you book."),
        ("How do PRINCE2 stages relate to sprints?", "A management stage usually contains several sprints and ends with a release or demonstrable increment. Making each stage a whole number of sprints means the stage boundary review looks at real output and an updated forecast rather than at documents alone."),
        ("What replaces a highlight report in an Agile team?", "Nothing needs replacing; it changes form. A short report built from the Sprint Review outcome, the burn-up chart, forecasts against tolerances and key risks gives the board what it needs without extra paperwork."),
    ],
